  "query_preview": "/WEDNESDAY THROUGH SUNDAY/...\n\nAnother H5 shortwave will round the base of the main longwave \nWednesday, traversing the area. Continued mid-level forcing for \nascent should lead to another round of showers and storms Wednesday \n(60-80%). Hires guidance shows the potential for training storms \nover the area, which with the continued ripe environment for \nefficient rainfall (PWATs of 1.9 inches, WCD of 4000m), this may \nlead to a heavy rainfall threat. The WPC currently has portions of \nsoutheast Nebraska into southern Iowa highlighted for a slight risk \nof excessive rainfall. By the end of Wednesday, storm total QPF will \nrange from a half inch to a little over an inch primarily along the \nPlatte River area into southwest Iowa. Cooler temperatures are \nexpected with highs in the low to mid 70s.\n\nLeading up to Saturday, should see the southwestern CONUS H5 ridge \namplify and push farther eastward toward the Plains. This will \nresult in generally dry conditions with a warming temperature trend. \nExpect highs to warm back to the low 90s by Sunday with a few areas \nin eastern Nebraska and southwest Iowa seeing heat indices in the \nlow 100s. Saturday could bring a slight chance (15%) for some \nshowers and storms as an H5 shortwave ejects towards the Plains area \nfrom the Pacific Northwest.",
